.TH DAQ-INSTALL-TOOLS 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daq-install-tools \- validate a DAQ release description and its install tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daq-install-tools
[\fB\-f\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-M\fR]
[\fB\-O\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daq-install-tools
reads a release description YAML, renders the base and test release
version strings from it, and checks that every path it names exists.
With \fB\-\-makedirs\fR it creates the install directories that are
missing.
.PP
Release versions are written as structured fields rather than as
strings, so they can be compared and re-rendered:
.PP
.RS
.nf
base_release:
  prefix: d
  major: 9
  minor: 0
  patch: 0
  suffix: ""
  path: /mu2e/releases/v9_00_00
.fi
.RE
.PP
which renders as \fBd09_00_00\fR. Numeric components are zero-padded to
two digits; an empty \fBsuffix\fR leaves no trailing underscore, and a
missing field falls back to the schema default, so a description that
pins only \fBmajor\fR still produces a usable string.
.PP
\fBinstall_path.basepath\fR is the install root, and every other key
under \fBinstall_path\fR is joined onto it, so \fBbin: "bin"\fR under a
basepath of \fI/home/mu2edaq/daq\-tools\fR means
\fI/home/mu2edaq/daq\-tools/bin\fR.
.PP
Note that this command validates and prepares; it does not itself copy
any files. Use
.BR install-login.sh (1)
to deploy into an account, or \fBcmake \-\-install\fR to deploy into a
prefix.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-release\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Release description to read. Default: the first
\fIcurrent_release.yaml\fR on the config search path. A worked example
ships as \fIconfig/current_release.example.yaml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-makedirs
Create the install directories that do not exist.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-override
Warn instead of failing when a release path is missing. Without it, a
missing base or test release path is fatal.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Report only; print what \fB\-\-makedirs\fR would create without
creating it.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the package version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The description is consistent, or \fB\-\-override\fR suppressed the
path problems.
.TP
.B 1
The description could not be read, a required field is missing, a
release path does not exist and \fB\-\-override\fR was not given, or a
directory could not be created.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the current release description:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-install-tools
.fi
.RE
.PP
Prepare the install tree, showing what would be created first:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-install-tools --makedirs --dry-run
daq-install-tools --makedirs
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect a description whose releases are not mounted here:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-install-tools -f config/current_release.example.yaml --override
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR create-environment.sh (1),
.BR install-login.sh (1),
.BR daq-read-config (1)
